/target
# Nested `target/` dirs from sub-crates that act as their own
# `[workspace]` (notably `tests/explicit-compile/kernel/`, which
# spirv-builder compiles via a forked nightly + spirv target).
# Also covers ui_test's per-fixture `target/ui/`.
**/target/
# Nested `Cargo.lock` files from kernel sub-crates that detach
# themselves via `[workspace]`. The root workspace's Cargo.lock
# stays tracked (root-anchored `/target` is excluded above, so
# this isn't ambiguous with the root lockfile).
**/kernel/Cargo.lock
Cargo.lock.*
*.swp
*.ppm
spikes/**/Cargo.lock
# scratch/ holds throwaway C reproducers (pocl event-race work). Keep the
# .c sources + diagnosis .md, ignore the compiled (extensionless) binaries.
/scratch/*
!/scratch/*.c
!/scratch/*.md
